{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1532637-scale-and-antagonists","id":1532637,"title":"Scale and Antagonists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-14T21:42:41-07:00","id":1532637,"title":"Scale and Antagonists","content":"As I understand it, their is two different Scale &quot;bonuses&quot; for antagonists:<br /> General ones, Durability, Leadership, Mental, Power, Might, Size and Speed.<br /> And specific ones, like the Centaur getting Scale 2 speed on unpaved ground or Scale 1 on paved roads.<br /> <br /> To what stats do you add Durability and Size?<br /> Of cause you add it to rolls where the antagonist can take advantage of their size, like hitting someone with a car.<br /> But would you add health boxes? Defence?<br /> And Durability, I seem to remember that it only adds +1 per scale, to defence, not the &quot;Dramatic&quot; bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3356-kalle","name":"Kalle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T05:13:52-07:00","id":1532999,"title":"","content":"Scales in Scion work slightly different from TC, specially Aberrant, where they are more rigidly defined.<br /> <br /> In Scion Scale apply when it apply, so if you say your hero antagonist is scale 2, he is not size 2, speed 2, etc, he is scale 2 where his titles and callings apply. A Warrior will apply to all the combat related because he is a warrior, while a Sage will apply on things related to his knowledge.<br /> <br /> An higher size scale usually have the same durability, Might and Power scales (using Aberrant terms) as its size, because its kind of part of its nature, but the point here is if you have a Size 2 objct, you hero will need to be size 2 to damage it without much difficulty.<br /> <br /> My suggestion is, if you have Scale over the target you gain 2e per scale, if the target have scale over you the difficulty increases by 2 (Defense is the difficulty of an attack), so if your Scale 2 Hero attacks a scale 0 target your hero gains 4e in the attack, if your hero attacks a scale 4 target the target defense increase by 2. This will automatically make it harder to cause damage to the target, so you dont need extra health.<br /> <br /> Notice that &quot;being scale 2&quot; doesnt means you have scale in everything, just means you will have scale when it is relevant to the situation. If the objective of the attack is disarming, the target scale may not apply if its caused by its heavy armor, because its not going to affect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T17:50:48-07:00","id":1533026,"title":"","content":"I unfortunately haven\u2019t had time to dive into Aberrant yet, but I am going to.<br /> Like Scale, Antagonists work a little different in Scion, then Trinity/Aberrant. Each Tier (Origin, Hero, Demigod and God) have a couple of Antagonist Archetypes, with their own dicepools, health, defence and initiative.<br /> <br /> In Scion Origin (page 65), Scale was divided into Size, Force, Speed and Leadership. In Scion Demigod (page 143), Scale was divided further into Durability, Leadership, Mental, Power, Might, Size and Speed.<br /> Scale evens out, in Scion as well, and you are right, that a Force 2 grenade would even out a car\u2019s Size 2 and a wall\u2019s Durability 2.<br /> <br /> But what I don\u2019t remember, and can\u2019t find in the books, is:<br /> A Scale Size 2 Troll adds a +4 enhancemen, when hitting a Scale Size 0 human, but would the Troll also add its Scale Size to its Defence or/and Health boxes, and is it by the entire +4 or only +2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3356-kalle","name":"Kalle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}